claims/CLAIMS.md:36:| A-INDEX-TC-fin | On a finite square-lattice toric-code torus with periods at least three, fix a proper contractible disk `D` and its joint electric/magnetic boundary PVM `{P_a(D)}`.  For a pure open ribbon `W_x` of type `x in Z_2^e x Z_2^m` whose active direct/dual components each have one endpoint inside `D` and one outside, `P_bW_xP_a=delta_{b,a+x}W_xP_a`.  Hence the enclosed endpoint has definite label `x`, the two-projective-measurement protocol using the same PVM twice is a probability law supported on `b-a=x`, and a closed probe `y` returns the nondegenerate braiding character `(-1)^(x_e y_m+x_m y_e)`.  The shift is invariant under ribbon deformations preserving the endpoint partition, but not under moving an endpoint across the circle or changing the measured circle. | **PROVED** | finite toric-code Pauli algebra | `theory/anyon-label-index.md` §§1--3 | `theory/checks/anyon_label_check.py` ANYON-C0--C4 and `--red wrong-sector` |
