**PROVE.** `e^{2πiρ}=c=e^{-2πiρ}`; hence `e^{4πiρ}=1` and `2ρ∈ℤ`.

**⟨2⟩1.** (IT phase slope = density.)  Put `f_α(θ):=θ_α(exp(θξ))`,
`V_θ:=V_α(exp(θξ))`, `u(θ):=e^{iθS^z}` on one site.  Then
`ω_α(u_x(θ))=e^{if_α(θ)}tr[V_θ^{-1}E_α(V_θ r)]`, and differentiating at
