./theory/lanes/blitz-2026-08-29/la-folium/lane.log:2433:theory/lanes/blitz-2026-08-29/ogata/lane.log:43:TASK: Deep dive — Yoshiko Ogata's operator-algebraic results in THIS context. Relevant corpus: her C*-index for SPT phases of quantum spin chains (H^2(G,U(1))-valued index via the split property), the classification of gapped Hamiltonians in 1D, the operator-algebraic Lieb-Schultz-Mattis theorems, the type-III half-chain factor structure, automorphic equivalence machinery. QUESTIONS: (1) Is our memory index / edge-charge quantization secretly (a corollary of / equivalent to / strictly different from) Ogata's SPT index? Map her split-property implementer to our D26 circle implementer (lane la-folium attacks the same object — note overlap, do not duplicate its proof). (2) Does her stability-of-index-under-automorphic-equivalence give us memory-index stability under the dynamical protocol FOR FREE (an (LR) hypothesis removal)? (3) Does the operator-algebraic LSM constrain which G/fillings admit our calibrated memory? GROUND TRUTH DISCIPLINE (L3): first `ls refs/` and use any local Ogata TeX; every attribution NOT backed by local TeX must be marked UNVERIFIED-NEEDS-FETCH with the arxiv id, and you never quote from memory as if verified. Output ogata-map.md: precise claim-by-claim correspondence table + the single best new theorem candidate it suggests, with a proof sketch.
./theory/lanes/blitz-2026-08-29/la-folium/lane.log:2434:theory/lanes/blitz-2026-08-29/ogata/lane.log:477:definitions.md:219:## D4 (bond implementers; effective asymptotic symmetry; charge algebra)
./theory/lanes/blitz-2026-08-29/la-folium/lane.log:2435:theory/lanes/blitz-2026-08-29/ogata/lane.log:633:claims/CLAIMS.md:87:| LR1-GEN | Let `𝔄` be the quasi-local algebra of a quantum spin system on a countable lattice with uniformly finite local dimension, `α_t` a strongly continuous one-parameter group of `*`-automorphisms of `𝔄`, `Ψ` a unit vector in any representation of `𝔄`, `c_0` a cut, and `Q̂_{W,c_0}∈𝔄_W` self-adjoint with finite spectrum at each finite window `W∋c_0`.  Then **every** prescribed sequence `S_n→∞` admits a subsequence `T_n=S_{n_j}` along which, **simultaneously for every such `W`**, the two Cesàro states `ω^±_{W,n}` converge weak-`*` on all of `𝔄` to states, and every double-Cesàro TPM weight `p_{W,n}(ν)` converges; each limit `p_W` is a probability supported in the finite set `spec Q̂_W − spec Q̂_W`, which under D26(INT) lies in `ℤ`.  This is D27's clause 1, so **clause 1 is a theorem, not a restriction — but it is not removable**: it existentially binds the single sequence that D27's clauses 2--3 quantify over, and the substantive content of `(LR)` therefore lies entirely in clauses 2--3.  The proof consumes exactly three inputs — separability of `𝔄`, strong continuity of `α_t`, finiteness of `spec Q̂_W` — and **no** spectral gap, Lieb--Robinson velocity, ergodicity, scattering or completeness input, and no property of `Ψ` beyond `‖Ψ‖=1` (per ⟨1⟩3.⟨2⟩7; ⟨1⟩3's ASSUME line still over-lists (H1),(H3) and is due a strengthening in a later round).  NOT claimed: pointwise-in-`t` convergence, which D27 does not ask for; convergence along the full sequence; anything about D27(LR2) or (LR3). | **PROVED** | D26, D27 | theory/lr-d16.md ⟨1⟩3.⟨2⟩1--⟨2⟩8, restated at ⟨1⟩6.⟨2⟩2 | theory/checks/lr_d16_check.py C1(a) TPM normalisation `6.66e−16`, C1(b) raw integer spectrum/support; green exit 0, `--red c1-nonunitary` and `--red c1-noninteger` each exit 1 on exactly that row.  These certify the finite-`W` TPM arithmetic only; **no gate bears on the Cesàro convergence itself**, which is not a finite-`N` testable statement and needs none — the proof is complete. |
./theory/lanes/blitz-2026-08-29/la-folium/lane.log:2436:theory/lanes/blitz-2026-08-29/ogata/lane.log:635:claims/CLAIMS.md:90:| M-INDEX-LA-folium | In the GNS representation of a FIXED A2/D1(e′) kink state, under D26(INT)+(S), the selected circle is implemented by a strongly continuous unitary group whose Stone generator `Q̂` has `e^{2πiQ̂}` scalar, hence pure point spectrum in one coset (implementer route; NOT a strong-resolvent limit of window charges, which ⟨1⟩12 refutes for nonscalar `V_θ`).  Evidence: O(1) twisted-transfer window-charge variance on the folium; local implementability of the rotation there.  **The entire content is EXISTENCE of the strongly continuous implementer** (NOTE 11 of memory-index-r2.md): once it exists and `ϱ_0` is pure, `e^{2πiQ̂}` implements `Ad(u(2π))=Ad(c𝟙)=id`, hence lies in `π(𝔄)'=ℂ𝟙` by Schur — the scalar clause is free, and a future prover should attack existence only. | CONJECTURE | A2, D26, D2(e) | theory/memory-index.md ⟨1⟩3b (markers: memory-index-r1.md objection 3(b)) | — |
